  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v14.0 - Breaking: validation failures use the ASP.NET Core shape (\"errors\" is a field-to-messages map, \"fieldErrors\" removed). Failures go through IProblemDetailsService (CustomizeProblemDetails applies) and always carry instance and traceId. New: \"code\" extension from WithCode, AddResultProblemDetails() for framework errors, ProducesResultProblem(...), and ResultProblemDetails/ResultValidationProblemDetails OpenAPI schemas. See CHANGELOG.md for migration.\n\nv13.3 - ProducesEnveloped<T>() / ProducesEnveloped(): documents the success body ToEnvelopedResult writes (OperationDataResult<T> or OperationResult) for OpenAPI, so API docs and generated clients see the envelope and its data type.\n\nv13.2 - ProducesResultProblems(): one call on a route group documents the Problem Details responses (500, 401/403 for authorized endpoints, 422 for endpoints with a body) for OpenAPI, with no extra package dependency. See CHANGELOG.md for full details.",
